Zero project format migration, 2026-11-17

The product source tree now contains authored Zero/Ezero code and owned data
containers. This cleanup removed historical generated executables, foreign
image files, raw test logs and temporary test devices. It did not rename PNG
or PPM bytes to a new suffix.

Image migration
572 P6 image files were encoded by tools/picture.zero into ZPIX0001 containers.
Every output passed the same native tool's verify command. The native raw
decoder reconstructed RGB bytes that were compared exactly with each original
P6 raster. All 572 pixel comparisons passed. The project now retains those
572 images as .zpix, including desktop views, 1080p tiled/scrolling views and
historical UI checks. Existing PNG duplicates and obsolete PNG-only fixture
screenshots were removed. No PNG/JPG/JPEG/PPM/GIF/BMP/WebP remain in the tree.
No audio or video assets were found; this report does not claim audio/video
codecs or playback support.

Historical reports
118 results, summary, status and review reports from old generated trees were
encoded into ZTEXT001 with the original Zero text utility. Every encoded report
was decoded and compared byte for byte with its original input before cleanup.
Other authored documentation is migrated by the documentation/checker tasks.

Removal scope
11,496 obsolete generated regular files were removed from the known build,
verification, candidate and test-output trees. This count includes old image
and text originals already converted above. An additional 19 media files
outside those trees, 19 obsolete UEFI test artifacts, 15 generated executable
files, 18 test symlinks and 7 test FIFOs were removed. Authored .zero, .ezero
and .zero.part files were retained, including regression test sources.
Three existing Zero source fixtures with a .zero.in suffix were given their
correct .zero suffix without changing their source bytes.

Protected data
Original own-format ZeroFS disk bytes moved from build/data.img to
data/storage.zdrive, SHA256:
c730241fb30f5516867c751006951a2878f360319195ee975411a05f040f27e8
The standard VirtualBox compatibility container moved outside the product to
/tmp/zero-support/user-data/data.vdi, SHA256:
7f58fb36c934405757da797ca65f2dddef3858e69107f43e2cae59d14c89bc5f
Both hashes match the protected originals. Neither disk was reformatted.

Bootstrap
bootstrap/zero64.zapp remains the original ZEROAPP1 compiler seed.
Old ELF bootstrap copies were removed from the source tree after confirming
the owned seed and current native compiler were available. Host ELF/PE and
firmware/optical compatibility exports belong outside this source tree.

At this checkpoint the only remaining non-owned suffixes were four top-level
documents assigned to the parent task: README.txt, WORKSTATE.txt, SHA256.txt
and verification.txt. No foreign source language files, shell shebangs,
symlinks or FIFOs remain in the product tree.
